menu "Presentation timer"

config COUNTER_PANEL_BENCHMARK
    bool "Run the panel timing benchmark at boot"
    default n
    help
        Times full and partial e-paper refreshes across a range of rectangle
        heights and logs the breakdown, then continues into the normal UI.
        Used to work out how much of a refresh is fixed overhead versus how
        much scales with area, which is what bounds how fast the clock can
        tick. Leave off for normal use: it delays boot by about half a minute
        and flashes the panel repeatedly.

config COUNTER_AUTOSTART
    bool "Start a short session automatically at boot"
    default n
    help
        Skips the setup screen and runs a compressed session (2 talks, 1
        minute each, 15s warning, 30s break) as soon as the device boots.
        Lets a whole session -- countdown, wrap-up, buzzer, break -- be
        captured over the serial log without anyone pressing buttons. Leave
        off for normal use.

endmenu
